    <string name="tracking_clock_explanation">Intervals follow the phone clock. A 30-minute interval targets :00 and :30, independently of extra wake, Location, or internet events. Each record keeps its reason, event time, intended clock slot, location measurement time, and database receipt separately.</string>
    <string name="tracking_clock_access">Clock timing / exact alarm access</string>
    <string name="tracking_clock_access_explanation">Exact alarm access helps Android wake the tracker at clock boundaries. Android and phone battery controls can still delay execution, and internet or GPS delays can delay delivery. The record shows its intended slot and actual event time. If no position is available, the event is still recorded without inventing coordinates. Open system settings to review access.</string>
